# FreeRTOS

- ISR: queue send or task notify only. No mutex, no log strings, no UDS.
- Watchdog task never takes a mutex. Missing heartbeat → do not kick WDT.
- Use mutex priority inheritance. Avoid priority inversion on the CAN path.
- Not every product creates every task (ESP32-C3 SRAM).
- Stack sizes in docs are targets until watermarks exist.

POSIX Virtual ECU should use the same task catalog via OSAL so queues/timeouts are testable without silicon.
